{
  "requirement": "Every {term}`requirements.sdk.application_domain` implements\n`trust_but_verify::domain::Domain`. A domain is cloneable and safe to share between\nexecutions. The following chapters introduce its members one capability at a\ntime:\n\n```rust,ignore\n// Defined in trust_but_verify::domain.\n/// Application data and operations used to evaluate criteria.\npub trait Domain: Clone + Send + Sync {\n    // ...\n}\n```",
  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "`requirements.sdk.domain` sets three testable obligations. Application domains implement `trust_but_verify::domain::Domain`. The trait is bounded `Clone + Send + Sync`, so a domain is cloneable. A domain is safe to share between executions. The reviewed tests cover each one.\n\n- **Trait and bounds.** `crates/trust-but-verify/tests/contracts.rs#fn[domain_relationships_accept_opaque_types_and_send_only_errors]` implements `Domain` for an opaque `Relationships` fixture. It also compiles a generic `check_bounds::<G: Domain>()` that demands `Clone + Send + Sync` of `G`. If the trait dropped any of those bounds, this would fail to compile. The comment says the test is meant to catch loosened bounds as well as added ones. The fixture is `Clone`, so it also rules out an added bound the fixture lacks. It also calls the trait's members through the trait.\n- **Cloneability in use.** `Validator::new(domain.clone())` is used in `contracts.rs#fn[criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested]` and `contracts.rs#fn[concurrent_same_criterion_executions_keep_complete_independent_records]`. The same call appears in `tests/validation.rs#fn[concurrent_single_node_validations_keep_separate_traces]` and in `src/agent/tests.rs#fn[behavioral_adequacy_uses_domain_contents_and_returns_a_typed_fingerprinted_answer]`. These tests then assert on results from the clones, including the shared state in `criteria_keep_typed_answers_and_persist_only_when_requested`.\n- **Sharing between executions.** Several tests run concurrent executions against one domain and assert on the outcomes:\n  - `concurrent_same_criterion_executions_keep_complete_independent_records` uses a barrier so both executions must run at once, then checks each record's revision and dependencies.\n  - `concurrent_single_node_validations_keep_separate_traces` checks that three concurrent validations peak at 3, and that each node's recorded dependencies are its own.\n  - `shared_context_allows_independent_concurrent_agent_calls` and `concurrent_tool_agents_isolate_histories_pages_and_submissions_and_share_reads` run concurrent agent calls against the shared domain.\n- **Usable as an application domain.** The other marked tests drive real `Domain` implementations through validation, evidence storage and agent calls, so the trait is exercised in realistic use. `src/sdk.rs#mod[tests]/fn[domain_formats_supplied_contents_without_resolving_a_replacement]` is also marked.\n\nThe requirement has no failure or boundary cases beyond these. The `rust,ignore` snippet only illustrates the trait declaration. I found no gap.",
  "references": "ed9ccc46ca7c14b9cdfc7ded9a2564da2295f3d6c8694a892bc5e88cc71c5a03",
